@startuml

title Client-Server Style Relationships

!include ../../../../../../tooling/styles/plantuml/structural/package-diagram-style.iuml

rectangle "Client-Server Style\n<size:9>Request/Reply, Asymmetric roles</size>" as CS $fill_primary

package "Specializes" {
    rectangle "Call-Return Style" as CR $fill_ok
}
note right of CR : General pattern\nCS adds role asymmetry

package "Composes With" {
    rectangle "Layered Style" as LAY $fill_caution
    rectangle "Pipe-and-Filter" as PF $fill_caution
    rectangle "Event-Driven" as ED $fill_caution
}
note right of LAY : Each layer\nserves layer above
note right of PF : Request processing\npipelines
note right of ED : Async messaging\ncomplement

package "Contrasts With" {
    rectangle "Peer-to-Peer" as P2P $fill_alt
}
note right of P2P : Symmetric vs.\nasymmetric roles

package "Implements" {
    rectangle "SOA" as SOA $fill_invalid
    rectangle "Microservices" as MS $fill_invalid
}
note right of SOA : CS between services
note right of MS : Services as both\nclient and server

CS -u-> CR : specializes
CS --> LAY : composes
CS --> PF : composes
CS --> ED : composes
CS <..> P2P : contrasts
CS -d-> SOA : implements
CS -d-> MS : implements

legend bottom
  | Relationship | Description |
  | Specializes | CS is a specific form of Call-Return |
  | Composes | CS combines with other styles |
  | Contrasts | Different approach to same problem |
  | Implements | CS provides interaction pattern |
endlegend
@enduml
